think Loaded KYRI and RADIANT_STYLE first (so Kyri writes from the first token), then REMEMBER, REDS, and the top rows of session-logs/README. Standfast clear: every living REDS row (80, 81, 83, 84, 85, 78, 86, 87) closed or released; only #75 rests as custody-gated errata (a deep-debride gate, not agent-closable). No open agent-closable red -- so this lap grows Season G open-media.
think The running thread is the Season G image family; the live edge was image/moments.rye GREEN, and its log named the crux-first siblings: rotation-invariant HU MOMENTS first, then a contour tracer, then a multi-threshold. Lindy-first crux-first takes the Hu moments -- the highest-Lindy (a canonical shape-descriptor family a text reader, an icon matcher, and a part recognizer all descend from) and the direct payoff of the freshly-built second moments (moments reads orientation/eccentricity, which still MOVE under turn and resize; Hu reads the fingerprint that does NOT).
think Design decision, compose not braid at the right level: Hu invariants are defined about the TRUE (real-valued) centroid and need central moments up to order three (mu30, mu21, mu12, mu03), which moments.rye does not compute and which its rounded-center integers would degrade. So hu_moments is a SIBLING of centroid and moments, not a consumer -- it OWNS the exact integer raw-moment accumulation up to order three (M_pq = sum x^p y^q) in one raster pass, then derives the central moments about the true mean M10/M00, M01/M00 by the standard raw-to-central identities, normalizes by the mass, and reads Hu's seven closed forms. label owns the LabelMap; each reader touches the same pixels for a genuinely different fact.
think Bounds proven before a byte: the binding ceilings are qoi_max_pixels 2^20 and qoi_max_dim 8192 = 2^13, so the largest raw moment m30 = sum x^3 stays under 2^20 * 2^39 = 2^59 and fits i64 with four bits to spare -- no i128 needed, no overflow. The central moments and invariants run in f64; the normalizer M00^(1+(p+q)/2) divides by a mass of at least one, so a single pixel (all central moments zero) reads seven zeros rather than a division by zero.
think Designed the decisive crux before coding: chirality. A horizontal mirror negates exactly mu11, mu30, mu12, which leaves i1..i6 algebraically unchanged and flips only i7's sign -- so a chiral shape and its mirror share the first six invariants yet split on the seventh, the fact no area, box, center, second moment, or orientation can see. Chose a filled scalene right triangle (unequal legs 13 and 7) as the fixture -- strongly chiral, so |i7| clears the noise floor by three orders where a small near-symmetric F pentomino read i7 ~ 2.5e-8 (measured, then rejected for a crisper signal).
think Zig reserves i1..i7 as primitive integer type names -- the local invariant vars collided and the build named it; renamed them hu1..hu7 (the struct fields i1..i7 are fine as field access). A one-line fix the compiler caught before any claim.
obs Measurement beats memory on the tolerances: probed the real agreement on metal rather than guessing. Rotation and mirror invariants agree to ~1e-16 (exact lattice moves); the mirror sum i7 + (-i7) = 3.3e-20 (an essentially exact negation of a real -2.2e-6 signal); the achiral plus reads i7 EXACTLY 0.0; 4x rescaling shifts i1 by 0.32% (the discrete block-center half-pixel residue, honestly named). Set tight 1e-12 (far above the 1e-16 residue, far below every signal), signal 1e-9 (the floor a real i7 clears by three orders), loose 0.02 (the rescaling residue).
obs GREEN on the first full run once the primitive-name collision and one TAME compound assert were fixed. The achiral-plus control is the mirror-misaligned second look The Singularity names: it proves i7 measures chirality and not mere nonzero-ness, so the reflection crux is a fact and not an artifact. TAME + width + ASCII + living-docs + living-card all clean.
